<node id="1232649" title="Re^2: Getting for() to accept a tied array in one statement" created="2019-04-16 09:12:09" updated="2019-04-16 09:12:09" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="1098601">perlancar</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;for (tie @ary, "My::Class", "some", "contents") { ... } # NOPE&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;does not work because for() gets a single-element list which is the tied object, not the tied array itself.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;code&gt;for (do { tie @ary, "My::Class", "some", "contents"; @ary }) { ... } #NOPE&lt;/code&gt;

&lt;p&gt;does not work because for() gets an ordinary (non-magical) list of values. All the values from the tied array have been FETCH-ed. I need to iterate over the tied array so code inside the loop block and FETCH are executed once for each element, together.

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;tie @ary, "My::Class", "some", "contents";
for (@ary) {
   ...
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;works, but I want something more similar to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;for (wrapper(@ary)) {
   ...
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;where @ary is an ordinary array or a list of values.&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
